MEDICAL CORPS -- PHYSICAL READINESS ASSESSMENT ("SAND ARMOUR" STANDARD)
Sunagakure Medical Division

"Sand Armour" is the corps' informal name for the baseline physical standard
expected of a field-ready Sand shinobi -- the discipline that lets a body endure
the desert as sand shields its user. This assessment is administered before each
extended deployment.

Assessed domains:
- Hydration efficiency and heat tolerance under graded exposure.
- Endurance over a supervised dune march with combat load.
- Chakra reserve and recovery, tested against sustained wind or puppet-thread
  emission for the relevant specialists.
- Injury history and old poison exposure (of note for Puppet Brigade members who
  handle live poison stock).

Grading: Pass returns the shinobi to deployment readiness; conditional pass
requires supervised reconditioning; fail refers to the medical corps for care.
Results are filed to the individual medical record and reported to the squad's
jonin. Maintained by the corps.
